{"name":"Frostwork","hex":"#eff1e3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frostwork","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any naturally occurring intricate pattern of ice crystals.","Any pattern that resembles a frost formation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frostwork"}],"entries":[{"title":"Frostwork (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, frostwork is a type of speleothem with acicular (\"needle-like\") growths almost always composed of aragonite or calcite replaced aragonite. It is a variety of anthodite. Frostwork can also be made of opal or gypsum. In some caves frostwork may grow on top of cave popcorn or boxwork."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Jewel_Cave_3.jpg/330px-Jewel_Cave_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frostwork_(geology)","wikidata":"Q4672016"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Popcorn-with-Frostwork.jpg/330px-Popcorn-with-Frostwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Popcorn-with-Frostwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Popcorn-with-Frostwork.jpg/330px-Popcorn-with-Frostwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APopcorn-with-Frostwork.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}